The Iceman, Plate I — Copperplate Engraving (Lemo-Opuscar)
A 31-second style sample: Ötzi, the man found in the Ötztal ice in 1991.
All drawings, lettering layout, animation, sound effects and music are original and generated by code in this folder.

MUSIC (music/score.py, original composition, D major, 96 BPM)
Harpsichord; solo violin, violins, violas, cellos, contrabass (pizzicato and arco).
Samples (CC0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition and the Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios).

SOUND EFFECTS
Synthesised in mix.py with numpy / core/audio/sfx.py: burin scrape and plate ring, swarf pings, press roller,
paper peel, granular hatching, pen scratch, water drop, wet brush, tissue rustle, room tone.

VOICE
Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_fable (en-gb).

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1, OFL.txt in fonts/)
Bodoni Moda (engraved roman capitals and italics) · Pinyon Script (copperplate script notes and subtitles).

FACTS (reference only, nothing traced or copied)
Copper axe, hide shoes over grass netting, unfinished yew bow — find inventory of the South Tyrol Museum of
Archaeology (iceman.it); radiocarbon date ≈ 3300 BC (~5,300 years).

STYLE REFERENCES (grammar only, nothing copied)
19th-century natural-history plates (Haeckel, Audubon, Westwood, the Encyclopaedia Britannica copperplates);
Hogarth and Doré for burin line and cross-hatching; hand-coloured plates for the watercolour washes.
The burin line engine (engine/) grew out of an earlier, unpublished LemoLab engine; everything it needs is in this folder.
